      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a bit vague, though. If I just tell them \"you're doing great, but buy this anyway,\" they're going to see right through it and probably decline. \n\nThe audit literally shows no major gaps. To make this landing actually work, we need a more \"urgent\" angle. Can we lean into the idea that while they're secure *now*, they're actually entering a high-risk window for specific types of attacks—like zero-days or lateral movement—that the current setup just isn't equipped to catch? I need something more concrete to justify the extra spend.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
